 "text": "Hi, how you doing right now? Sorry to hear that. Try to arrive as early as you can, even if it' just few minutes. Lots of people check in right at the last minute, so the order can get mixed up. Best to wait. The bride and groom will still be busy with their own family and guests. You can stand near the entrance and watch from there. Try to leave bit early and see you can cut across parkland if there's no police tape. A short walkway beats rushing in traffic. You' get see everyone arrive, the officiant introduce everyone, and sometimes a child or two will be brought in. Then find a seat near the front and enjoy the ceremony.",
